+# HARNESS_LOG — dasha predictions error
+
+## Plan
+- Report: opening a dasha period's predictions shows an error; "worked before, stopped recently".
+- Read: app/api/dasha/route.ts, lib/claude.ts, lib/constants.ts, lib/claude-models.test.ts.
+- Finding: `generateDashaPrediction` (lib/claude.ts) sends an assistant prefill message
+  (`{ role: "assistant", content: "{" }`) to MODEL_PRIMARY = "claude-sonnet-5". The route's own
+  comment says prefill was removed "because newer Claude models reject it" — but the call
+  still uses it. The API rejects the request → route catch → 500 "Dasha prediction failed".
+  "Stopped recently" fits the model upgrade to Sonnet 5.
+- Fix: drop the prefill; return text via `jsonReplyText` (same as the other JSON calls, also
+  surfaces max_tokens truncation clearly). The route already runs `prepareJsonString` to
+  extract the JSON object, so no route change needed.
+- Add a regression test under lib/ asserting no call in lib/claude.ts ends with an assistant
+  prefill message.
+- Run: npx vitest run, npx tsc --noEmit.
+
+## Log
+- Change 1: lib/claude.ts `generateDashaPrediction` — removed assistant prefill `"{"` and the
+  `"{" +` re-prepend; returns the text block. (Kept lenient extraction instead of
+  `jsonReplyText` so a max_tokens-truncated reply still reaches the route's regex fallback.)
+- Change 2: added lib/claude-no-prefill.test.ts (regression guard).
+- `npx vitest run` → Test Files 38 passed (38), Tests 282 passed (282).
+- `npx tsc --noEmit` → no output (clean).
+- Not run: confirming the new test fails against the old lib/claude.ts (git stash needed
+  approval). Reasoned only: old source contained `role: "assistant"`, which assertion 1 matches.
+- Not run: a live call to the Anthropic API / the running app.
